   <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-indent: 0px; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; margin-left: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-top: 6pt;"><tbody><tr style="vertical-align: top; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;"><td style="width: 2%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;"> <p style="margin: 0pt; font-size: 8pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;"><sup style="vertical-align:top;line-height:120%;">(a)</sup></p> </td><td style="width: 98%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif;"> <p style="margin: 0pt; font-size: 8pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; text-align: justify;">Basic and diluted earnings per share are calculated using actual, unrounded amounts. Therefore, the quarterly earnings per share <em style="font: inherit;"> may </em><em style="font: inherit;">not</em> sum to the earnings per share on the Consolidated Statements of Operations.</p> </td></tr>
</tbody></table>
   <p style="margin: 0pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt;">&#160;</p>
